description:
src/event.rs:14-18 doc-comment on handle_calendar_event_get:

    /// Handle a CalendarEvent/get method call (draft-ietf-jmap-calendars-26 §5.4).
    ///
    /// Extra args (`expandRecurrences`, `reducedParticipants`, `fetchCalendars`)
    /// are passed through to the generic handler which forwards them to the
    /// backend via the args `Value`.

Three problems:
1. The section reference is wrong: §5.4 is the per-user properties section. CalendarEvent/get is §5.7 (line 1417 of the draft).
2. The arg names are wrong: spec defines recurrenceOverridesBefore, recurrenceOverridesAfter, reduceParticipants (no 'd'), and timeZone. There is no expandRecurrences on /get (that's /query §5.11) and there is no fetchCalendars in the draft at all (a search of the draft text returns 0 hits).
3. The claim 'are passed through to the generic handler which forwards them to the backend via the args Value' is wrong — the args go through but the generic handler does not consume them, the backend never sees them, and the typed CalendarsBackend trait has no plumbing to receive them. See JMAP-r3pg.2 for the production bug; this is the parallel doc bug.

This doc-comment will mislead any future contributor who reads it as the contract for /get extra args.

Fix: rewrite with correct §5.7 reference and correct arg names. State honestly which args are currently dropped (until JMAP-r3pg.2 lands) and which are forwarded.

Severity: P3 because doc accuracy. Bumps to P2 once anyone implements a backend trusting this doc.
